Quevra contracts package — license overview
==========================================

This package is **multi-licensed by file**. The `SPDX-License-Identifier` at the
top of each Solidity source is authoritative for that file. Do not treat the
package as uniformly MIT or as uniformly open source.

License texts
-------------

- `LICENSE-MIT` — MIT License for Quevra-authored sources and for MIT-licensed
  adaptations that retain upstream notices.
- `LICENSE-BUSL-1.1.txt` — Business Source License 1.1 terms for files whose
  SPDX identifier is `BUSL-1.1` (adapted from Mezo Earn / Tigris).
- Dependency licenses remain with their packages (notably OpenZeppelin MIT under
  `lib/openzeppelin-contracts` / npm `@openzeppelin/*`, Foundry `forge-std`, and
  `monad-std`).

What applies where
------------------

| Category | SPDX | Text |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Quevra-authored protocol, staking, and tooling sources | MIT | `LICENSE-MIT` |
| Adapted Tigris sources that upstream marks MIT | MIT | `LICENSE-MIT` plus notices in the file / `docs/provenance.md` |
| Adapted Tigris sources that upstream marks BUSL-1.1 | BUSL-1.1 | `LICENSE-BUSL-1.1.txt` |
| Tests, scripts, and docs without an SPDX header | MIT, unless they embed or require a BUSL source | `LICENSE-MIT` |

BUSL-1.1 is **source-available**, not an OSI open-source license. Production use
of BUSL-covered files is limited by that license unless and until an upstream
Change Date converts them under the stated Change License.

Per-file provenance, upstream revisions, and adaptation notes are recorded in
`docs/provenance.md`.
